# CODEOWNERS
#
# This file maps paths in the repo to whoever should review changes to them.
# GitHub auto-requests a review from the matching owner(s) when a PR touches
# a given path.
#
# Handles below are pulled from the repo's Collaborators list (Settings >
# Collaborators). A few people don't have a confirmed handle yet (pending
# invite, or not matched). See the TODOs below.
#
# HOW GITHUB APPLIES THIS FILE (read before editing):
#   - For a single file, only the LAST matching pattern in this file counts.
#     Patterns don't stack for the same file. Order matters; more specific
#     patterns should come after more general ones.
#   - Across a whole PR, if different changed files match different owner
#     groups, GitHub requires at least one approval from EACH distinct group
#     represented, e.g. a PR touching both frontend/ and backend/ needs one
#     approval from Frontend AND one from Backend.
#   - Within one line/group, only ONE of the listed owners needs to approve
#     to satisfy that line. GitHub can't natively express "this person AND
#     that person" on a single path. See the gatekeeper note below for how
#     we're handling that gap.

