# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gatekeeper rule: Lin and Shauna (build coordinator + GitHub admin)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Policy (can't be fully expressed in CODEOWNERS syntax, see note below):
#   At least one Frontend teammate must approve frontend PRs, and at least
#   one Backend teammate must approve backend/Open Liberty PRs. IN ADDITION,
#   if neither Lin nor Shauna was that approver, one of them should also
#   approve before merge.
#
# Why this isn't just written as a rule below: GitHub only requires ONE
# approval from the full list of owners on a matching line. It can't
# require "teammate X" AND, conditionally, "teammate Y unless X was already
# Y." Lin (@linthantaung-gif) and Shauna (@shkeating) are included in the
# Frontend/Backend owner lists above so they're auto-requested on every
# relevant PR, but satisfying this policy for real is on reviewers, not
# automation, until we either:
#   (a) turn on branch protection requiring 2+ approvals overall on
#       protected branches (a blunter tool, doesn't guarantee it's
#       specifically Lin/Shauna), or
#   (b) move to GitHub repository rulesets, which can require review from
#       multiple distinct code-owner groups on the same path.
# Until (a) or (b) is set up, reviewers should manually check: "did Lin or
# Shauna approve this?" before merging Full Stack PRs.

